WEBVTT

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.700
Ow...

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:15.750
Huh?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.140
Mimi, bring me a glass of water.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:28.150
Okay!

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.050
There you go.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.970
Vodka means water in Russian.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.460
Besides, you prefer this to water, don't you?

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:08.160
Now that you're more cheerful,
let's do our best at work!

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.370
You have to take your job seriously!

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.070
Job, huh?

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:28.720
I keep telling you that you should get an eye exam.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.140
It's the same as before, right?

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.640
But it may have gotten worse.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.620
Of course not.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.510
Huh?

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:38.400
Bye.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.790
Hey, Rin-chan.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:10.420
I saw that the truck was about to hit a cat,
and then its tanker exploded.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.990
Where did that cat go?

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:13.990
No clue.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.120
It went that way.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:16.190
Thank you.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.050
Excuse me...

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:29.550
Hey!

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:31.720
Come with us!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.630
You know why, right?

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.130
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:35.430
Hey, wait a minu—

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:41.490
Please stop this!

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.510
Shut up and come with us!

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.820
Wait.

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:48.890
Y-You bitch!

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:56.920
Let's go.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.240
Eh?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.240
Wh-Where?

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.310
My, are you asking a lady this?

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:02.830
Ow...

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.050
Shouldn't we run?

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.910
I hate running.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.020
Rin!

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.420
Didn't you go looking for a cat?!

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:22.480
I brought back a man instead of a cat, as you can see.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.130
Yeah, make yourself comfortable.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.770
Our house is your house.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:28.610
Okay...

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.690
All right...

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:30.690
And?

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.570
"And?"

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:33.990
What happened?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.800
Well, I don't really know either.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.090
I don't know why they tried to pick a fight with me.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:44.610
I apologize for getting you involved.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.330
It's just...

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:46.670
Just?

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:50.670
I had a feeling you could help me.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.900
You're always bringing back guys like this, Rin.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.680
Is her name Rin-san?

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.130
Yes.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:02.390
And I'm Mimi, forever.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:04.920
And?

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.670
Um, well...

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.150
Who am I?

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.650
Do you have amnesia?

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.590
No, I have my memories.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:20.810
My name is Maeno Kouki.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.900
I remember my address and phone number as well.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.850
Even what I had for dinner last night.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.670
But I don't have any emotions.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.690
It's a strange feeling.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:37.210
I'm sure that I'm Maeno, but I somehow can't confirm it.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.550
How should I say it?

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:42.950
It's as if I'm pretending to be someone else.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:44.270
Then...

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.930
Do you have any idea who attacked you?

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:49.710
Not the slightest clue.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.900
When I came to, there I was, standing around.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:56.400
Even though she doesn't look it, Mimi is older than you.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:02.010
You have no idea why you were in Kabuki-cho, right?

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.480
It's not like that.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.070
I don't have any memory of that.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:09.360
If I recall correctly, I left the house this morning and went to the university.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.960
And when I came to my senses, I was there.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:15.170
Okay.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:16.170
Yes?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:17.920
Let's leave it until tomorrow.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.040
Sorry?

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.210
Again?

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:23.140
Don't leave for tomorrow what you can do today.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.060
U-Um...

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:28.560
Let's drink.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:35.090
If you drink now, that weird feeling may be gone when you wake up.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.030
Okay...

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:36.930
Yep, yep.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.210
Cheers!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.520
To the destined meeting.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:46.530
C-Cheers.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.870
Ah, what a waste.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:55.540
A drop of alcohol is equal to a drop of blood.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:56.270
R-Right.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:17.190
Yes?

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:21.490
Yes.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:24.530
You're right.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.140
Yes.

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:27.950
Huh?

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:34.540
Can you see it?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:36.540
Right.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:39.740
Maybe it's closer than we expected.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.050
Good morning.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.790
I see you have a hangover.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.060
You were drinking with us, after all.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:55.840
Here.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:56.870
Thank you.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:11:58.950
This is...

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.420
There's brandy in it.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.380
The best drink for a hangover.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.220
How are you?

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.480
How do I feel?

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.040
I still feel sick.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.570
I didn't mean that.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.040
Do you feel like your real self?

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.020
I guess it was no use after all.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.620
You seem physically normal, though.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.920
Well then, let's go.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.050
Where?

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:25.930
To find you.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.220
Maeno Kouki, twenty years old.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.500
Sophomore at Joukou University, economics major.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.760
Father: Maeno Kiyoshi.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.250
Mother: Ryouko.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:38.090
That's correct.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:39.720
Maeno, huh?

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.350
It's a strange feeling somehow.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:51.700
Although it's my house,
I don't feel like I was born and raised there.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.680
And when I look at my mother, she feels like a stranger.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.610
She doesn't seem to be worried about you.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:01.880
I often sleep at my friends' houses without telling her.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.910
Your friends' houses, huh?

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.230
Male friends.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:08.520
Really.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.230
Wh-What the hell?!

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.890
They don't seem to have driver's licenses or ID cards.

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:45.890
I wonder if they're professionals.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:47.640
P-Professionals?

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:51.170
At coercion, extortion, abduction, and so on.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:55.600
If they're professional thugs,
I won't be a match for them.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.580
Ueyama Estates?

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.530
Hey, Rin-chan.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.100
Yo.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.000
Do you feel like working with us?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.190
Of course not.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:16.260
Being a domina isn't really my taste.

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:19.040
That part would sell like hotcakes...

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:20.160
Do you know him?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.420
I'm sure you know that information doesn't come cheap.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.430
How about the whereabouts of that girl you're looking for?

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.440
You know where she is?

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:30.890
Please tell me!

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.740
That girl—

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:32.930
You first.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.900
Ueyama Estates, huh?

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.720
Where have I heard that before?

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:43.930
Okay, okay...

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:44.990
I don't know.

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:48.860
It must be a dummy company for some group.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:49.700
What?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:52.590
That aside, tell me where she is!

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:54.000
When I feel like it.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.450
I beg you, Rin-chan! She's deep in debt!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.280
Rin-chan!

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.180
Bro.

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.800
Tamotsu!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.130
Over here!

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:10.480
You idiot!

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.140
If someone sees—

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.400
Welcome.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:14.680
A blended coffee, please.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:15.730
Right away.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.960
What if someone sees us?!

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:20.740
Will they think you're being immoral?

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.040
I'm single.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.550
You know that, don't you?

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.890
W-When did you...?!

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:30.740
Just kidding.

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:35.250
Don't scare me like that.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.180
And who's this guy?

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:38.370
It's a bit complicated.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:40.850
Regarding the matter we discussed on the phone...

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:45.460
How can a police officer tell you something like that?!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.530
Oh?

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.540
Then, I'll tell what you did last year...

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.580
I got it.

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.920
On the surface, Ueyama Estates
is a reputable medium-sized company.

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.100
Actually, it's a front for the Chino group.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.950
Are they yakuzas?

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:01.640
Then, why do they have a good reputation?

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:04.610
Do something about this kid.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.520
I'm not your teacher.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.100
I can't teach you everything from scratch.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.710
It's all right to ignore him.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.200
Does the Chino group have connections to other companies?

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:16.880
They are connected to many big companies.

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.870
If you're careless, you'll get your fingers burned.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.900
They have especially deep connections in real estate.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.320
They're better known as land sharks.

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:31.040
Kakubishi Estates and Misutomo, to name a few.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.620
Companies like Aoyama Pharmaceutical,

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.400
Toyama Industrial Enterprises, and Sky of Japan,
are involved as supporters.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:37.800
Aoyama Pharmaceutical?

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.660
Did you remember something?

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:40.260
Yes.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.320
About a month ago,

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:47.010
if I recall correctly, my senpai introduced me to them because they paid well...

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.720
and they were testing a new drug.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.130
I guess I'll give it a shot.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:02.620
Hey!

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:06.150
I don't know what you're involved in this time,

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.490
but use a little discretion.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:08.940
Thanks for the advice.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:09.960
You're always so kind.

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:13.640
I-It's not like that!

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.430
This is the Managing Director of Nakayama.

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.150
Ah, hello.

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:19.110
I'm pleased to meet you.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.620
What a pity.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:59.400
That was our chance to get to know each other better.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.680
As expected from a Managing Director.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:27.350
He did everything by the book.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.270
I hear you can't die...

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:37.080
I can't die because I'm a bad person!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.250
I see...

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:43.130
Then, I'll kill you again and again!

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.700
Room service.

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:04.350
Should I leave it in front of the door?

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:07.410
Or should I bring it back later?

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:09.780
Can't talk right now!

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:25.670
Who's your client?!

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.070
Apos?

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:29.680
Answer me!

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:34.710
The anonymity of the client is absolute!

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:50.490
I shot you!

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:55.080
Good people die prematurely.

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:25.190
Y-You are...

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:46.500
Geez...

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:49.370
If you're hungry, there's food in the fridge.

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:50.470
Oh, come on.

00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:53.230
Something bad happened after all?

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:54.350
Beats me.

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:57.370
Don't do anything weird.

00:22:57.370 --> 00:22:59.120
Maeno-kun is looking at us.

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:00.070
Yeah, yeah.

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:01.230
And how did you do?

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:01.850
A cat?

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:04.710
I couldn't find much.

00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:07.320
The mail files were corrupted,
so I couldn't check the contents.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:10.930
But it seems there was a lot of mail traffic
between the Sayama Research Institute

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:14.620
and Aoyama Pharmaceutical on the day
you brought Maeno-kun here.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:21.520
The Sayama Research Institute doesn't ring any bells.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:24.060
Guess we'll have to confront them head on.

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:31.520
Will this be all right?

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:34.300
Trust Mimi's skills.

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:34.930
But...

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:40.420
Is something the matter?

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:45.060
It's nothing.

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:50.940
Are you...

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:53.070
How should I say it?

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:53.840
Different?

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:55.670
I'm sorry.

00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:56.750
It's okay.

00:23:56.750 --> 00:23:57.180
No...

00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:00.740
And you got involved in all this because of me...

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:01.700
Don't worry about it.

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:04.710
It's a bit late, but who are you guys?

00:24:05.230 --> 00:24:07.820
Jacks of all trades, I guess.

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:10.040
And what about repayment?

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:10.950
You mean money?

00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:12.770
Oh yeah, I'll think about that.

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:15.020
Good work.

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:16.220
Please wait there for a moment.

00:24:30.830 --> 00:24:32.030
Did he find out?

00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:39.230
You look much prettier in person.

00:24:39.760 --> 00:24:41.090
Thank you very much.

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:49.250
So?

00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:51.250
Do you remember anything?

00:24:55.270 --> 00:24:56.720
Welcome.

00:24:56.720 --> 00:24:59.640
Hey you, this way.

00:25:00.620 --> 00:25:02.640
I walked straight along here.

00:25:07.400 --> 00:25:08.620
Hey, what's wrong?

00:25:08.620 --> 00:25:09.110
Maeno-kun?

00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:29.960
Did you remember something?

00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:30.460
Yes.

00:25:32.500 --> 00:25:33.020
This way.

00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:44.480
Judging from your state,
something happened here, right?

00:25:44.480 --> 00:25:45.120
Yeah.

00:25:46.260 --> 00:25:47.970
Now is your only chance to turn back.

00:25:49.790 --> 00:25:52.650
You asked me who you were.

00:25:53.680 --> 00:25:57.150
Perhaps you can find the answer here.

00:25:57.150 --> 00:25:59.920
But you might be better off not knowing.

00:26:00.780 --> 00:26:01.970
The decision is up to you.

00:26:04.020 --> 00:26:04.760
I...

00:26:06.200 --> 00:26:07.050
want to know.

00:26:07.890 --> 00:26:11.170
No, I feel that I have to know.

00:26:12.660 --> 00:26:13.340
Okay.

00:26:13.920 --> 00:26:15.410
Then it's a deal.

00:26:15.410 --> 00:26:16.170
Is something wrong?

00:26:16.620 --> 00:26:19.680
Oh sorry, he's feeling sick.

00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:22.800
Could he rest somewhere?

00:26:24.570 --> 00:26:28.510
I'm sorry, but outsiders aren't allowed to enter my room.

00:26:28.510 --> 00:26:29.260
It's okay.

00:26:29.260 --> 00:26:31.600
We were gonna check this room too.

00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:34.320
We'll take care of it once he feels better.

00:26:34.550 --> 00:26:35.720
Okay. Bye.

00:26:37.580 --> 00:26:39.980
Could you lend me a cigarette and a lighter?

00:26:42.020 --> 00:26:42.740
Sure.

00:26:44.630 --> 00:26:45.680
Thank you.

00:26:45.680 --> 00:26:47.720
I'll bring it back to you later.

00:26:47.720 --> 00:26:49.210
Hurry up and finish your job.

00:26:49.210 --> 00:26:50.310
Yes, thank you.

00:26:51.790 --> 00:26:52.500
The coast is clear.

00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:52.920
Okay.

00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:56.040
The guard was carrying a gun.

00:26:57.150 --> 00:26:59.010
From here on, it'll be dangerous.

00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:00.120
Yes.

00:27:01.200 --> 00:27:03.440
According to the blueprints Mimi provided,

00:27:03.440 --> 00:27:04.390
the second floor seems suspicious.

00:27:05.170 --> 00:27:08.550
However, we'd have to pass through the security officer's room.

00:27:09.050 --> 00:27:10.440
So this is the only choice.

00:27:34.010 --> 00:27:35.780
Light the cigarette.

00:27:36.490 --> 00:27:37.340
O-Okay.

00:28:09.780 --> 00:28:10.170
Um...

00:28:10.170 --> 00:28:11.780
Say one word and I'll hit you!

00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:38.240
I'm Yamanobe Sayara.

00:28:38.750 --> 00:28:40.710
Just call me Sayara.

00:28:40.710 --> 00:28:41.940
Saya is fine, too.

00:28:42.830 --> 00:28:43.950
And you are...?

00:28:43.950 --> 00:28:45.110
Oh, it doesn't matter.

00:28:45.110 --> 00:28:46.200
I'll find out soon enough.

00:28:48.710 --> 00:28:52.960
Say, do you know how many holes a human body has?

00:28:52.960 --> 00:28:55.520
Two for the eyes, two for the ears,

00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:58.290
two for the nose, and one for the mouth.

00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:00.830
And three here.

00:29:00.830 --> 00:29:01.710
Ten holes in all.

00:29:02.530 --> 00:29:04.490
Though men have only nine.

00:29:05.150 --> 00:29:08.930
Through piercing, men can change the number of holes that God gave them.

00:29:10.030 --> 00:29:15.550
Since ancient times, men have used piercing to differentiate themselves from God's creation.

00:29:15.550 --> 00:29:16.440
Don't you think so too?

00:29:18.340 --> 00:29:19.190
It looks good on you.

00:29:20.080 --> 00:29:22.340
Or should I put it here?

00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:24.540
It'll make your body clean.

00:29:25.950 --> 00:29:29.990
From now on, I'll pierce you bit by bit.

00:29:29.990 --> 00:29:31.700
And do many other things, as well.

00:29:32.940 --> 00:29:34.330
You're such a sadist.

00:29:37.620 --> 00:29:40.000
My, are you scared already?

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:41.670
But don't be.

00:29:41.670 --> 00:29:43.090
Don't speak yet.

00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:48.990
I don't want to hear that kind of voice to start with.

00:29:53.210 --> 00:29:55.580
First, the eleventh hole.

00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:28.340
Hey, you're going to die.

00:30:29.870 --> 00:30:30.890
Pretty soon.

00:30:38.330 --> 00:30:39.270
At...

00:30:40.490 --> 00:30:41.710
At Shinjuku...

00:30:42.510 --> 00:30:45.640
The tanker accident...

00:30:46.980 --> 00:30:48.320
It was transporting Maeno-kun...

00:30:48.810 --> 00:30:49.400
Yes.

00:30:49.970 --> 00:30:52.130
It was awful, from what I heard.

00:30:52.130 --> 00:30:54.590
We had to go through all the trouble of deceiving the police,

00:30:54.590 --> 00:30:56.540
because it was a special vehicle for transporting a test subject.

00:30:57.220 --> 00:31:00.040
The head office is full of idiots.

00:31:00.040 --> 00:31:02.290
It's their fault for taking him away from me.

00:31:02.780 --> 00:31:05.640
It was against their recommendation, my foot.

00:31:05.640 --> 00:31:07.320
Why Maeno?

00:31:08.520 --> 00:31:11.800
Very well... I'll tell you.

00:31:12.710 --> 00:31:14.850
He's a compatible clone.

00:31:16.660 --> 00:31:18.840
I'm an expert in bacteria.

00:31:19.460 --> 00:31:21.330
I have discovered that a certain RNA bacterium

00:31:21.330 --> 00:31:25.820
interacts with human DNA and multiplies rapidly.

00:31:26.910 --> 00:31:29.540
Thus, I transcribe the information in the brain.

00:31:29.540 --> 00:31:29.860
How—

00:31:30.500 --> 00:31:31.490
How did I do that?

00:31:31.490 --> 00:31:33.640
That's a company secret.

00:31:34.140 --> 00:31:36.240
Well, it's not done through machines.

00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:38.370
And the quantity of information is enormous too.

00:31:38.370 --> 00:31:41.500
The development of the software would have taken forever.

00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:43.660
It's done through chemistry.

00:31:44.330 --> 00:31:46.670
Doing something like that...

00:31:46.670 --> 00:31:48.100
You ask why?

00:31:48.100 --> 00:31:50.200
It's the first step to becoming immortal.

00:31:54.310 --> 00:31:55.390
What's so funny?

00:31:58.190 --> 00:32:01.850
Did Apos trick you?

00:32:02.810 --> 00:32:03.860
Apos?

00:32:04.680 --> 00:32:05.360
Who are you talking about?

00:32:06.360 --> 00:32:07.730
Am I wrong?

00:32:09.280 --> 00:32:15.780
Really, humans are so persistent about becoming immortal.

00:32:18.490 --> 00:32:24.300
Did you know... some people are so proud they turn into monsters if you make them mad?

00:32:25.160 --> 00:32:28.010
Especially if you make fun of their research.

00:32:32.550 --> 00:32:34.930
Ah, the chief's terrible, isn't she?

00:32:34.930 --> 00:32:36.230
This is a real mess.

00:32:36.230 --> 00:32:38.110
And she was a real babe.

00:32:38.110 --> 00:32:40.590
Violating her like this...

00:32:40.590 --> 00:32:42.240
Let's take care of it.

00:33:05.310 --> 00:33:06.730
It's all right now.

00:33:07.290 --> 00:33:10.610
The person who brought you here is already dead.

00:33:10.610 --> 00:33:12.850
Thank you for coming back.

00:33:12.850 --> 00:33:14.970
I'll never let go of you again.

00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:20.050
No matter what the bosses say, okay?

00:33:56.080 --> 00:33:56.510
Ow...

00:34:16.140 --> 00:34:16.690
Good.

00:34:31.520 --> 00:34:32.960
There appears to be another intruder.

00:34:33.680 --> 00:34:34.660
Take care of it.

00:34:34.660 --> 00:34:36.060
You have permission to shoot.

00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:36.550
Yes ma'am.

00:34:38.520 --> 00:34:43.220
I don't know who it is, but that person better not go into the experimental area.

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:47.390
And I hate all this running...

00:34:50.350 --> 00:34:51.190
Damn!

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:06.830
Evacuate!

00:35:06.830 --> 00:35:08.250
Hurry up and evacuate!

00:35:58.290 --> 00:36:01.340
So what she said was true.

00:36:02.770 --> 00:36:04.990
Maeno-kun... he's...

00:36:12.310 --> 00:36:13.170
Hang in there.

00:36:13.170 --> 00:36:14.160
Can you talk?

00:36:36.670 --> 00:36:37.810
I have locked the door.

00:36:37.810 --> 00:36:38.730
What about the cameras?

00:36:38.730 --> 00:36:41.240
Reception in Section B was poor to begin with...

00:36:41.240 --> 00:36:42.950
Oh, what a shame.

00:36:42.950 --> 00:36:44.820
So much for showtime.

00:36:44.820 --> 00:36:47.410
Are we really opening that area?

00:36:48.700 --> 00:36:50.810
P4 separated. Unlocking the door.

00:37:19.440 --> 00:37:20.710
You people...

00:37:28.720 --> 00:37:32.120
You people were turned into this by Sayara...

00:37:36.280 --> 00:37:38.810
Yes... you're no longer...

00:37:46.990 --> 00:37:49.280
I'll bring you peace now.

00:38:06.030 --> 00:38:08.050
To think that the barrier wall of Section B would break...

00:38:08.850 --> 00:38:10.770
The contamination will leak in here as well.

00:38:10.770 --> 00:38:12.460
What should we do?

00:38:12.460 --> 00:38:13.190
Let's see...

00:38:13.860 --> 00:38:16.460
Take the important documents from A to C.

00:38:17.180 --> 00:38:19.850
We'll burn this place down and Section B with it.

00:38:20.970 --> 00:38:22.780
B-But if we do that, the main office will...

00:38:24.160 --> 00:38:27.210
Don't underestimate it,
just because the rate of infection is low!

00:38:28.020 --> 00:38:29.950
Or do you want to end up like them?

00:38:30.820 --> 00:38:31.600
U-Understood!

00:38:46.600 --> 00:38:47.070
Who's there?!

00:38:59.550 --> 00:39:00.040
No way!

00:39:00.540 --> 00:39:02.030
You're supposed to be dead!

00:39:02.940 --> 00:39:03.980
No way!

00:39:31.020 --> 00:39:32.510
You're right.

00:39:36.810 --> 00:39:37.850
I did die.

00:39:39.230 --> 00:39:39.740
Ouch!

00:39:39.740 --> 00:39:41.760
It hurts! It hurts!

00:39:41.760 --> 00:39:44.710
No! Mama! Mama!

00:39:44.710 --> 00:39:45.570
I am...

00:39:48.550 --> 00:39:50.070
what you are trying to achieve.

00:39:51.020 --> 00:39:52.260
This can't be...

00:39:53.760 --> 00:39:54.950
H-Help me...

00:39:54.950 --> 00:39:55.530
Help me...

00:39:56.120 --> 00:39:56.860
Help me!

00:40:04.010 --> 00:40:05.610
I hate to say this, but...

00:40:05.610 --> 00:40:05.910
Please open the door!
I hate to say this, but...

00:40:05.910 --> 00:40:06.910
Please open the door!

00:40:06.910 --> 00:40:12.150
life is something transient, and you shouldn't toy with it.

00:40:20.560 --> 00:40:21.340
This is...

00:40:22.290 --> 00:40:23.210
What was I...?

00:40:27.170 --> 00:40:28.570
Let's go back.

00:40:40.380 --> 00:40:41.190
Am I...

00:40:42.240 --> 00:40:43.940
a clone?

00:40:45.110 --> 00:40:47.720
Was that why I couldn't feel anything?

00:40:49.880 --> 00:40:52.100
What should I do now?

00:41:00.110 --> 00:41:01.280
Decide for yourself.

00:41:02.440 --> 00:41:05.690
I won't say that I understand your pain.

00:41:06.460 --> 00:41:09.190
Your pain is something only you can understand.

00:41:09.920 --> 00:41:11.020
I can't understand it.

00:41:12.770 --> 00:41:16.270
I won't tell you that you're trying to run away from that pain.

00:41:17.220 --> 00:41:19.420
Because that's another way of being saved.

00:41:22.730 --> 00:41:26.540
Living with the burden of that pain
or escaping from the pain...

00:41:27.550 --> 00:41:28.540
Decide for yourself.

00:41:29.800 --> 00:41:31.460
Because it's your life.

00:41:36.680 --> 00:41:39.050
Thank you very much for saying that.

00:42:27.350 --> 00:42:28.300
Hey...

00:42:28.740 --> 00:42:29.730
aren't you drinking?

00:42:30.810 --> 00:42:31.520
No...

00:42:35.070 --> 00:42:38.780
That's why you should've picked up the cat instead of a man.

00:42:39.790 --> 00:42:40.340
Yeah.

00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:42.620
I do regret it.

00:42:42.620 --> 00:42:43.520
Coming!

00:42:47.450 --> 00:42:48.930
You...

00:42:48.930 --> 00:42:51.300
Rin!

00:42:53.710 --> 00:42:57.970
I'm the only one who can live my life.

00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:04.680
So... can I work here?

00:43:06.820 --> 00:43:08.190
Employment decided!

00:43:13.020 --> 00:43:14.010
Let's drink.

00:43:14.010 --> 00:43:16.580
Yay! Let's drink!

00:43:17.510 --> 00:43:20.400
Come on. We're celebrating!

00:43:20.400 --> 00:43:21.640
Let's celebrate!
